id=a52sxq_appcloud_guard
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: no stock /prism OOBE app pushers
author=kusti420
description=Samsung's stock CSC partition /prism (not part of this ROM, left on the phone by the stock firmware; which of its APKs a phone installs depends on the sales code) carries third-party OOBE app pushers. Classified from the pulled APKs: app pushers/installers = ironSource/Aura "AppCloud" com.aura.oobe.samsung.gl (global; HOME intent at priority 4 = pops up right after setup, Galaxy Store attribution receiver) + com.aura.oobe.samsung ("Orange Manual Selector", same SDK) + com.ironsource.appcloud.oobe.hutchison ("Three AppCloud", INSTALL_PACKAGES); Digital Turbine Ignite "Mobile Services Manager" com.dti.telefonica + com.dti.tim; Orange "App Center" com.orange.update (INSTALL_PACKAGES); Altice/SFR "My Apps" com.altice.android.myapps.samsung and "My Games" com.sfr.android.sfrjeux.samsung; Deutsche Telekom "App Starter" (CombinedStarter) de.telekom.tsc (INSTALL/DELETE_PACKAGES); Facebook preload stub com.instagram.android (preloaded-stub, com.facebook.appmanager family). Not pushers, left alone: "Chili Companion" tv.chili.companion.android and Amazon "Mobile Device Information Provider" com.amazon.appmanager (MDIP) are content providers only (preload attribution data, no installer code). Build: the pusher APK names go on PackageManager's skip list (/system/etc/skipping_apk_exceptions.xml, read with the CSC's enforceskippingpackages.txt at every boot including the first one) and the pusher package names are dropped from allowed-system-preload-apps.xml (second gate: "Package is not in allowed list"), platform.xml, deviceidle/reviewed_allowlist.xml, default-permissions-platform.xml and the OMC LogiaDeck grants. Boot: /system/bin/k4-appcloud-guard (root, shell domain, sys.boot_completed, log tag k4-appcloud-guard) drops a /data update and uninstalls each listed pusher for user 0; stubs only while they are still the untouched /prism stub; fallback only for system packages in the com.aura.oobe/com.aura.jet/com.ironsource.appcloud/com.ironsrc.aura/com.dti/com.digitalturbine namespaces. Nothing outside those names is ever touched. Setup wizard: SecSetupWizard has no AppCloud hook of its own (the pusher hijacks HOME at priority 4), the Store's omcagent "recommended apps" step is removed separately by unica/mods/setupwizard.
